\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2002\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 5 (Reuters) - The world's biggest pile of foreign reserves grew even larger in June as dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to push up the country's official reserve assets by $26.5 billion to a record $446.198 billion. \par \par \uc2  The rise in the value of the euro and higher valuations for the government's massive holdings of U.S. government bonds were also major factors, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The rise was caused by the fact that we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," a senior MOF official told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities, concerned that a strong yen could derail \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led recovery, have repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since late May to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimate that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent the equivalent of $18.56 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. \par \par \uc2  Most of the dollars bought would have been used to buy U.S. Treasury bills and notes, they said. \par \par \uc2  Japan held $363.384 billion in foreign bonds at the end of June, up from $337.366 billion a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury bond fell to about 4.75 percent in late June from slightly over five percent at the beginning of the month. \par \par \uc2  The capital gain on the U.S. Treasury paper would be reflected in Japan's external reserves. \par \par \uc2  The euro's gain against dollar, which would boost the dollar value of the euro-denominated foreign reserves, also added to the rise in foreign reserves in June. \par \par \uc2  The euro climbed to a high of $0.9941 on June 26 from the month low of $0.9312 on June 3. Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose about 6.8 percent against the dollar during the month. \par \par \uc2  The ministry does not disclose the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  make-up of its official reserves, but analysts and traders believe that more than 70 percent is held in in dollars. \par \par \uc2  Japan had $65.466 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits at the end of June, down from $65.966 billion a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Gold holdings fell to $7.84 billion from $8.04 billion. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020705dy7500ez8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
