\par\par \b \uc2  IMF Chief Koehler Hints At Action On Dollar - FT \b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2002\par 01:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The International Monetary Fund could seek international coordination of exchange rates if nervousness in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets led to a run on the dollar, Horst Koehler, IMF managing director, signaled, according to a Financial Times report on its web site Friday. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with the Financial Times, Koehler said he was cautious about advocating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but, if the dollar were to fall rapidly and in a disorderly fashion, "no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all is not the right answer". \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen by 12% against the euro since January, almost reaching parity last week. On Thursday, it rose slightly, ending European trading at $0.9793 to the euro, the FT said. \par \par \uc2  But risks to the dollar continue as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remain nervous about the state of the US economy and, in particular, the current account deficit, the FT said. \par \par \uc2  The last time exchange rates were coordinated was in September 2000 when \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowed the slide of the euro. The current US administration has been opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maintaining that the market should determine exchange rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The IMF supported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 1980s through the Plaza and Louvre international agreements but large-scale global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management fell out of favor in the 1990s. \par \par \uc2  Koehler welcomed the dollar's fall and the rise of the euro, saying the dollar had been overvalued. He doubted the dollar would go into freefall, because Europe was not yet an alternative to the US as a source of growth and demand for capital. \par \par \uc2  "The US economy is more flexible than others, which makes us believe that the US economy may rebound strongly," he said, according to the FT. \par \par \uc2  Threats to financial stability weren't confined to developing or poor countries, he said, citing the demise of Enron, the energy trading company, and WorldCom, the telecommunications group, as factors undermining confidence. \par \par \uc2  Koehler was confident that the weakness in international stock markets could be overcome, although he recognized that much of the losses were due to the exaggerated euphoria of the late 1990s. \par \par \uc2  Pointing to the underlying strength of financial sectors, he said he expected old economy stocks to demonstrate "their solidity in terms of accounting and good corporate governance". \par \par \uc2  Koehler warned that the role of governments and the IMF was not to bail out the private sector in periods of financial difficulty. "We can't have a world where excessive profits are reaped and then, all of a sudden, the IMF or states have to repair the damage," he said, according to the FT. \par \par \uc2  Koehler was also critical of "hypocrisy and double standards" among industrialized countries regarding trade barriers to developing countries and subsidies to industries such as textiles and agriculture. \par \par \uc2  He called on the US and the European Union to ensure that the Doha trade round would genuinely be a "development" round and would focus on increasing developing countries' access to rich countries' markets. \par \par \uc2  Too often the US and EU made deals among themselves and gave preferential treatment to their favorite countries but this was not the route to liberalization of world trade, he said, according to the FT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020704dy7400178\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
