\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen; Hayami Comments Spark Buybacks \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2002\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar rose against the yen in Asia Thursday on short-covering sparked by unusual rhetoric from Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami that indicated Japanese monetary authorities are united in their efforts to stem sharp rises in the yen. \par \par \uc2  In his semiannual report to parliament, Hayami said sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are a danger to Japan's economy, suggesting that even Hayami - a well-known yen-bull - is adhering to the Finance Ministry's stance that it won't let up on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  "If fluctuations are too sudden, it could lead to instability in financial markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. That could have a negative effect on the economy," Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  Since May 22, the Finance Ministry has conducted seven rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the strong yen from snuffing out the nation's nascent economic recovery. Last Friday, it sold yen via the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in its recent series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also boosted against the yen by heavy selling of euros for dollars by foreign banks and speculators during the Asian session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro/dollar's plunge also lifted the dollar/yen today," said a Japanese city bank dealer, citing lingering concerns about the financial health of Vivendi Universal, the French entertainment giant. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y120.35, above Y119.92 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y120.09 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9758, lower than $0.9799 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9828 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y117.40, down from Y117.51 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y118.00 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Ahead of the national holiday in the U.S. later in the global session, some U.S. and other foreign banks bought back the dollar against the euro, in order to square positions. \par \par \uc2  But overseas and local speculators sold euros for dollars, aiming to trigger rumored stop-loss sales orders around $0.9770 and $0.9760, which they did. The euro dropped to an intraday low of $0.9751. \par \par \uc2  "There are more stop-loss sales orders rumored to be around $0.9750. If these are triggered, the euro could fall further toward the $0.9700 level," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Amid expectations for the euro to continue its short-term correction, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could easily trigger those orders later in the global session, which may push it below the psychological important $0.9700 level and into the mid-$0.9600s, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro lost some ground but was supported by buying from Japanese institutional investors planning to purchase euro-denominated securities. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5263, up from $1.5258 in New York, but lower than $1.5309 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020704dy740007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
