\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Slips Against Dollar But Bulls Undaunted \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Soble \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2002\par 07:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro gave up more ground against the dollar in Asia Tuesday, edging below $0.9850 after coming within hair's breadth of parity with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Monday's Asian session. \par \par \uc2  But market players said the single unit's retreat would be temporary, as traders were merely selling the euro to hedge against an unexpected fall in the short term. In the big picture, the euro is still heading higher and is sure to rise over the one-dollar wall before long. \par \par \uc2  "This is a temporary adjusting of positions," said Aozora Bank chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Shuji Takano. "But I don't see long-term change, and there's still a lot of room for the dollar to fall." \par \par \uc2  In Asia Monday the euro hit a high of $0.9974, but slipped below $0.9900 in subsequent New York trading. That slide was the main reason why some traders figured it might be a good idea to hedge short-term downside risk, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar regained some ground against the yen, grinding up to the Y120 mark it broke briefly above Monday. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's trading range was narrow, as widespread bearishness kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed down, while the specter of more yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again put a floor under the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The gloomy outlook for U.S. stocks prevented today's dollar gains from igniting general optimism toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Ripples of last week's stunning accounting disclosures at WorldCom Inc. and Xerox were still being felt this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the Nasdaq Composite Index closed at its lowest level in over five years after falling 4.06%, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average slid 1.44% to its weakest close since Oct. 31 last year. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see investors regaining confidence in U.S. stocks anytime soon," said a Japanese city bank trader. "Without that, the dollar's only heading downward." \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y120.00, above Y119.87 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y119.45 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9829 lower than $0.9898 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $0.9942 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y117.97, down from Y118.65 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y118.76 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5244, down from $1.5316 in New York and lower than $1.5331 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials continued to pitch their view that the weak dollar threatens the global economy. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said his ministry's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, conducted through the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reflected the opinions of foreign central bankers regarding the sliding dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The fall (in the dollar) from Y130-Y131 to Y125 in a span of three, four days, and a further fall below Y120, was excessive for anyone," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the seventh by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late May, was the first to involve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities outside Japan. \par \par \uc2  Although the U.S. and European central banks didn't add their own funds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the coordinated action was seen as an effort to show that Japan isn't alone in its fight against dollar bears. \par \par \uc2  Administrative Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Mutoh said Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "a step forward" for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy - perhaps a hint to markets to expect more such cooperation in the future. \par \par \uc2  But later in the day U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill downplayed Friday's move, emphasizing that the Fed had merely facilitated the yen-selling. He said he remained "agnostic" on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs a strong dollar to fuel its vital export industries. But Japanese officials, it seems, have a long way to go before they convince the rest of the world to close ranks behind the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074