\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar resists bears, takes heart from firm data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2002\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 2 (Reuters) - The dollar put up resistance to its quarter-old downtrend on Tuesday morning, aided by strong U.S. manufacturing data and wariness about more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spearheaded by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar sentiment improved after the U.S. Institute for Supply Management reported on Monday its index of U.S. manufacturing activity rose to 56.2 in June from 55.7 in May. That was better than the 55.8 expected on average by economists polled by Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The data helped the dollar hold firm in U.S trade despite a fall in U.S. share prices - a rare shift of focus for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that have been obsessed with the health of Wall Street in recent months. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's firm tone carried over into Asian trade, where the greenback edged up to 119.85 yen from 119.65 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro slipped nearly half a cent to $0.9872/77 from $0.9916 in late U.S. trade. It also eased against the yen, to 118.28/46 yen from 118.66. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was susceptible to profit-taking after its rapid and almost relentless rise in recent weeks. It gained more than five percent versus the dollar in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  A correction was inevitable with its 14-day relative strength index - an indicator of short-term balance of positions - shooting up to 92 on Monday, well above the 70 mark, which indicates a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is overbought. \par \par \uc2  "Because the euro has risen so rapidly, those who had bought euros are now selling them," said Tomomasa Noguchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was firm against the Swiss franc, sterling and Australian dollar, which all took a beating from profit-taking after hitting multi-month highs last week. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc eased to 1.4879 franc per dollar from 1.4814 in late U.S. trade. The Australian dollar fell to $0.5597 from $0.5624, while sterling slipped a little to $1.5304 from $1.5325. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS \par \par \uc2  Wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has grown acute since the BOJ enlisted the help of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve for its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time for the BOJ to enlist outside help in its latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign - which began in late May - to stop the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  "Before Friday, the market thought there was disaccord on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies among world policy-makers," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Though Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - in which central banks use their own reserves - it suggested U.S. and European authorities were at least not opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's initiative, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar could stay in a range between 118 and 121 yen for the time being," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Tuesday that overseas monetary authorities accepted Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through them last week because the dollar's steep decline had become a global issue. "As I have been saying, if the dollar drops from 130-131 yen toward 125 within a span of three, four days and further goes beyond 120, it's a rapid move in anyone's eyes," Shiokawa told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary authorities cannot just idly sit and watch. That's why we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Separately, Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka said the yen may be overvalued, which some dealers said marginally weighed on the yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0306 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 01 Jul.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9872   0.9916   -0.44   +10.87   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               119.76   119.65   +0.09    -9.02   131.63\par  Euro/yen              118.24   118.66   -0.35    +0.85   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.4880   1.4814   +0.45   -10.33   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.5302   1.5325   -0.15    +5.23   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5178   1.5157   +0.14    -4.64   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5597   0.5624   -0.48    +9.62   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4694   1.4695   -0.01    -0.58   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6449   0.6469   -0.31    +5.32   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020702dy720073n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngb