\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Moves Slightly Higher Against Major Counterparts \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry and Tyler Lifton \par \uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2002\par 00:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -- After incurring steep losses last week, the dollar held its ground Monday, grinding modestly higher against its major counterparts even as U.S. equity markets again slipped into negative territory. \par \par \uc2  But the gains were largely seen as a mere pause for the dollar before it continues its descent against the world's major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a trend that has dominated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the euro was at 98.98 U.S. cents, lower than the 99.14 cents level registered late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar was at 119.87 yen, up from 119.60 yen late Friday in New York. Against the Swiss Franc, the dollar was at 1.4841 Swiss Francs late Monday, above late Friday's 1.4825 francs, while against the British pound, it was at $1.5316, little changed from the $1.5311 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The theme continues to be the weak dollar. The key question is how far it could go," said Larry Kantor, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at JP Morgan. But he said the economic data this side of the Atlantic continues to outshine that in the euro zone and Japan, which should help ward off a straight-line descent in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the dollar may have gleaned some support from a key reading of manufacturing sentiment, the Institute for Supply Management's purchasing managers index, which moved to 56.2 in June after having stood at 55.7 in May and 53.9 in April. Readings above 50 indicate expansion of activity and prices in the manufacturing sector, while readings under 50 denote contraction. \par \par \uc2  Economists had expected the factory sector to have grown at virtually the same pace as the prior month. The weakening dollar was cited as a factor behind the recent U.S. manufacturing strength. \par \par \uc2  And the latest Tankan survey out of Japan showed that sentiment among big manufacturers improved for the first time in a year and a half, reflecting relief among managers that business conditions are getting better as stronger exports power a rebound in production. \par \par \uc2  The report initially gave the yen a boost versus the dollar. However, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost ground to the greenback later in the session as concerns over the effect of a stronger yen on Japan's economy as well as concerns about future Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen took hold. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the survey showed that companies expect the dollar to average 125.73 yen in this fiscal year to March. That is higher than the 124.21 yen average rate that companies forecast in the March report, even as strategists' outlook for the dollar has become increasingly bearish in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the release of a slightly disappointing euro-zone purchasing managers' report, which showed the main index rising to 51.8, somewhat less than the 52.0 average forecast, caused the euro to stall versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  All in all, however, the latest economic releases had a muted effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Instead, a consolidation of positions ahead of the July 4 holiday and an expected respite to the dollar after its headlong tumble last week were behind the day's price action. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think much of the data right now because no one's looking at it," said Jeremy Fand, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Friedberg Mercantile Group in New York. Instead, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market professionals are more concerned with the stock market and the widening U.S. current account deficit, he said. \par \par \uc2  But while the direction of the stock market has been a good indicator of the dollar's fate in recent sessions, the gains in the greenback Monday were perhaps more notable precisely because that was not the case. Both the Dow Jones Industrial Average and the Nasdaq Composite ended deep in the red, but the dollar managed to hold on to some gains, although it slipped back a bit during the afternoon session as equity losses deepened. \par \par \uc2  Partly reflecting global concerns about the weakness of asset prices, particularly stocks, due to U.S. corporate accounting blow-ups, a number of central banks meeting this week will likely decide to hold rates steady for now, said Tim Stewart, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Morgan Stanley in New York. Those meeting include the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of England, Sweden's Riksbank and the Reserve Bank of Australia. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the victory by its soccer team in the World Cup Sunday, the Brazilian real hit another record low around 2.900 Brazilian reals against the dollar Monday, before rebounding slightly to trade at 2.896 reals late in the New York day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness reflects "continued uncertainty about the [presidential] election results in Brazil...[and] global spillover from a very negative market environment in the U.S.," said Lara Rhame, senior economist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York. \par \par \uc2  "International capital is really drying up and that's a huge vulnerability to Brazil," because it has a budget deficit and needs to roll over its debt, she said. \par \par \uc2  Write to Tyler Lifton at tyler.lifton@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2002 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020701dy71006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
