\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Kuroda: Can't Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 02:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- A top Finance Ministry official reiterated Monday that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is unchanged, effectively warning that the authorities remain prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem an excessive yen rise. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda also said that he couldn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh time since May last Friday via its accounts at the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Federal Reserve Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said he didn't think the improvement in business sentiment shown in the Bank of Japan's tankan survey Monday would drive the yen higher. \par \par \uc2  "That's because the global economy is recovering steadily," he said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's June tankan showed sentiment among big manufacturers improved for the first time in a year and a half, reflecting relief among managers business conditions are getting better as stronger exports power a rebound in production. \par \par \uc2  The closely watched sentiment index for big manufacturers improved to minus 18 from minus 38 in the March survey, the biggest improvement on record. \par \par \uc2  The index measures the percentage of companies saying economic conditions are good minus the percentage saying conditions are bad; fence-sitters are ignored. \par \par \uc2  At 0116 GMT, the dollar was trading around Y119.69, above a nine-month low of Y118.36 hit Friday. \par 