\par\par \b \uc2  O'Neill confirms Fed  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  Friday for  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 17:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  UNITED NATIONS, July 1 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill confirmed on Monday that the U.S. Federal Reserve Board had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday on behalf of the Japanese government. \par \par \uc2  O'Neill, speaking with reporters at United Nations headquarters after addressing the U.N. Economic and Social Council, said he had no opinion on such actions as it should be up to individual governments to set their own policy. \par \par \uc2  "The Federal Reserve didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own behalf. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the request of the Japanese government, which is not unusual," he said when a reporter asked him how he felt about what the reporter referred to as Friday's Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "And I continue to be agnostic about that issue. Governments need to do what they believe is the right thing for them," O'Neill said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020701dy7100u4k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pic