\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bears pause as U.S. stock futures gain. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 1 (Reuters) - The dollar steadied a cent away from parity with the euro on Monday as signs Wall Street would weather a slew of recent corporate accounting scandals halted the greenback's recent slide. \par \par \uc2  Worries further dubious U.S. corporate practices might come out of the woodwork after news of improper accounting at Xerox and WorldCom last week allowed the euro to make another attempt at the one-to-one level earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  But the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned tail as U.S. stocks futures turned higher and dealers took heed of more warnings from Japan that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  muscle could be deployed again to calm unruly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  "The market needs to see further negative news on U.S. corporate governance to push the dollar lower," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has already fallen very sharply and looks oversold on a short-term basis." \par \par \uc2  The greenback fell to nine-month lows against the yen and 28-month lows against the euro on Friday before aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted it off its lows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned that the yen's recent surge against the dollar could derail its nascent export-led recovery and on Friday asked the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said nervousness that Japan might order further yen selling was supporting the dollar at 119.90 yen , up a quarter-percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro pulled back to $0.9900 by the European midsession, after rising as high as $0.9977 earlier in the session. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been under broad-based selling pressure since early April as doubts over the strength of the U.S. recovery and the reliability of U.S. accounting standards have dimmed the once-unrivalled appeal of U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  While euro zone politicians have generally welcomed the dollar's fall against the euro, Japanese policy-makers have been troubled by the threat that a less competitive exchange rate poses to Japan's fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  Japanese vice finance minister Toshiro Muto suggested on Monday that the country's decision on Friday to enlist the help of other central banks could be a step towards more coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi, meanwhile, warned that Japan was always in contact with overseas monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  "At present, coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks unlikely but we are certainly closer to this scenario than we have been for some time," said Mitul Kotecha, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that even some euro zone policy-makers were now sounding more cautious about the speed of recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  European Union Monetary Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes was quoted on Saturday as saying a stronger euro was good for the euro zone economy but that the speed of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the dollar was worrying. \par \par \uc2  ECONOMIC DATA WATCH \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were awaiting U.S. manufacturing data later in the day to clarify the state of the world's largest economy. \par \par \uc2  The June ISM survey, formerly known as the NAPM, is due for release at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The euro showed little reaction earlier to a survey showing a slight pick-up in manufacturing activity in the euro zone. The Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index rose to 51.8 in June from 51.5 in May. \par \par \uc2  Retail sales figures for the euro zone were less upbeat, with sales unexpectedly falling 0.6 percent in April from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The market also showed little reaction to the Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" corporate sentiment survey for June, which came in much better than expected. \par \par \uc2  Market players said they were concerned the survey did not fully take into account the recent rise in the yen and the weakness of the domestic stock market. \par \par \uc2  The survey's closely watched diffusion index for major manufacturers came in at minus 18, an improvement of 20 points from the previous March survey, the biggest gain on record. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020701dy7100ny0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
