\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar weak versus euro, corporate worries weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 12:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 1 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped within half a cent of the psychologically-important parity level with the euro on Monday, dogged by continued investor disillusionment with U.S. asset markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders were looking to how Wall Street would fare later, after the latest U.S. accounting scandal involving Xerox Corp on Friday left investors worried what other accounting irregularities might come out of the woodwork. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is very vulnerable to further crises of confidence in U.S. asset markets," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services. \par \par \uc2  "People are almost treading water waiting for parity to happen." \par \par \uc2  The greenback fell to nine-month lows against the yen and 28-month lows against the euro on Friday before aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted it off its lows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned that the yen's recent surge against the dollar could derail its nascent export-led recovery and on Friday asked the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said nervousness that Japan might order further yen selling was keeping the dollar supported at 119.75 yen , up marginally on the day. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retained a weak bias against the euro at $0.9925 , having fallen as low as $0.9977 earlier in the session. \par \par \b \highlight22