\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar fades, supported only by BOJ fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazunori Takada \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 09:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 1 (Reuters) - Worries over the fragile U.S. stock market continued to plague the dollar on Monday, with only fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  preventing the greenback from a rapid fall, traders said. \par \par \uc2  On top of a sluggish Wall Street, the latest U.S. accounting scandal involving office equipment group Xerox Corp was also undermining the bearish sentiment, they said. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, though, traders said the dollar looked to be shielded by wariness over more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday through the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) for the first time during its selling of yen over the past two months. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that we saw the Fed and the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ was surprising, but again, the impact was limited as the dollar dipped about one yen from the high," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lifted the greenback to 120.40 yen from a nine-month low of 118.36 yen, but resistance proved stiff. \par \par \uc2  At 0551 GMT, the dollar was buying around 119.45 yen against Friday's late U.S. level of 119.59. Market participants said they were reluctant to chase it significantly below 119.50, seen as a level where the BOJ could step in. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained in sight of parity against the dollar, at 99.35 cents compared with 99.05 in late U.S. trade on Friday. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaked at a 28-month high of $0.9985 on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 118.64 yen up from 118.53 yen. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said Japan was always in contact with overseas monetary authorities, but he declined to say whether it had any plans for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least six days since late May, concerned that a stronger yen would derail an export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Banking sources have estimated the BOJ may have bought $18.56 billion in its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. \par \par \uc2  LITTLE REACTION TO TANKAN \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly "tankan" corporate sentiment survey for June, which came in much better than expected. \par \par \uc2  Market players said they were concerned that the survey did not fully take into account the recent rise in the yen and the weakness of the domestic stock market. \par \par \uc2  The survey's closely watched diffusion index (DI) for major manufacturers came in at minus 18, an improvement of 20 points from the previous March survey, the biggest gain on record. \par \par \uc2  "The headline figures were impressive. But considering that the recent yen rise and stock falls were not accounted for, I think the actual picture for corporate sentiment should be weaker," Nomura's Toyahara said. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, the market's focus is not on Japan's fundamentals, but on fading confidence in the United States," he added. \par \par \uc2  The performance on Wall Street, above all else, will be the focus in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. stock prices will be more important for the market than economic indicators," a trader at a major Japanese bank said. "Depending on its performance, we may see a change in the recent sell-dollar sentiment." \par \par \uc2  Among key U.S. economic data due out this week is the unemployment rate for June on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0553 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   28 Jun. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9935   0.9915   +0.20   +11.58   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen        119.49   119.57   -0.07    -9.22   131.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    118.71   118.43   +0.24    +1.25   117.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.4792   1.4807   -0.10   -10.86   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr        1.5323   1.5333   -0.07    +5.38   1.4541\par  Can/dlr        1.5160   1.5185   -0.16    -4.76   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr        0.5605   0.5633   -0.50    +9.77   0.5106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4702   1.4679   +0.16    -0.53   1.4780\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6480   0.6463   +0.26    +5.83   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...  Debt... Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \