\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar remains under pressure over US corporate woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 1 (Reuters) - The dollar remained under pressure in Tokyo on Monday as pessimism over the U.S. equity market made dealers nervous about building new long positions despite official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the greenback last week. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the dollar was undermined further by a new U.S. accounting scandal after office equipment group Xerox Corp discovered a $2.0 billion revenue gap in its books. \par \par \uc2  But wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided support for the dollar after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday through the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) for the first time during its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the past two months. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that we saw the Fed and the EBC \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ was surprising, but again the impact was limited after the dollar dipped about one yen from the high," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  The central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ after the greenback dropped to a nine-month low of 118.36 yen. The dollar rose as high as around 120.40 yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but faced stiff resistance around that point, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As of 0329 GMT on Monday, the dollar was quoted at 119.55/57 yen against Friday's late U.S. level of 119.59/69. \par \par \uc2  The euro remained in sight of parity against the dollar, trading around 99.50 cents compared with 99.05/10 in late U.S. trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaked at a 28-month high of $0.9985 on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "My impression is that the dollar's topside is getting heavier and heavier. Despite (Friday's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar's topside has been stuck around 120.50 yen," a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be nervous about selling the dollar too strongly following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but given the basic bearish trend, the dollar is still vulnerable to speculative selling." \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Monday that Japan was always in contact with overseas monetary authorities, but he declined to say whether it had any plans for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occasions since late May because of concern that a stronger yen would derail an export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Banking sources said on Friday that the BOJ was estimated to have bought $18.56 billion in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. \par \par \uc2  LITTLE REACTION TO TANKAN \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to the BOJ's quarterly "tankan" corporate sentiment survey in June, which came in much better than expected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was concerned that the survey did not fully reflect the recent rise in the yen and the weakness of the domestic stock market. \par \par \uc2  The survey's closely watched diffusion index (DI) for major manufacturers was at minus 18, an improvement of 20 points from the previous March survey, the biggest gain on record. \par \par \uc2  The result of the survey of 8,550 companies, taken from May 30 to June 28, was better than financial market forecasts. A Reuters poll of 20 economists had predicted that the widely watched index would come in at minus 26. \par \par \uc2  For large non-manufacturers, the tankan's headline diffusion index rose to minus 16, up from minus 22 in March and beating economists' forecasts of minus 20. \par \par \uc2  "The headline figures were impressive. But considering that the recent yen rise and stock falls are not counted, I think the actual picture of the tankan should be weaker," Toyahara said. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, the market's focus is not on Japan's fundamentals, but on fading confidence in the United States itself," Toyahara added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 118.89/98 yen compared with 118.53 yen in late U.S. trade. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0338 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   28 Jun. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       0.9946   0.9915   +0.31    +4.74   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen        119.48   119.57   -0.08    +4.39   114.45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    118.80   118.43   +0.31    +9.28   108.71\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.4776   1.4807   -0.21    -7.72   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr        1.5334   1.5333   +0.01    +2.23   1.5000\par  Can/dlr        1.5153   1.5185   -0.21    +1.60   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr        0.5604   0.5633   -0.51    +0.18   0.5594\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss  1.4691   1.4679   +0.08    -3.48   1.5221\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg    0.6485   0.6463   +0.34    +2.53   0.6325\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...  Debt... Indicato