\par\par \b \uc2  WRAPUP 1-Japan recruits ECB and Fed to help weaken yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2002\par 17:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 28 (Reuters) - Japan enlisted the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve to help sell yen on Friday to prevent the surging Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from snuffing out Japan's export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen against the weakening dollar on at least three days this month and three days in May but the yen has continued to gain against the greenback, hitting a nine-month high earlier on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda told Reuters. "The ECB and Fed are operating on behalf of the BOJ as well." \par \par \uc2  The dollar leapt more than one yen to above 120.30 yen from 118.90 shortly before the action. The euro jumped from around 118 yen to around 118.80. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda added: "We will continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets carefully and take appropriate action as needed." \par \par \uc2  A Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the ministry could not comment on which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, an ECB spokesman confirmed it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of Japanese authorities, buying euros against the yen. \par \par \uc2  In London, the Bank of England decline to comment on whether it had taken part in the action. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank said it had not been involved. \par \par \uc2  Japan's action to cap yen strength last September proved relatively successful as it coincided with a broad-based rally in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  This time, however, the greenback is under heavy pressure across the board. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020628dy6s00u3h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
