\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles but cushioned by BOJ wariness. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2002\par 08:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 28 (Reuters) - The dollar stayed on the defensive on Friday amid doubts about Washington's commitment to its official strong-dollar policy and the fragile U.S. stock market, but caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited selling. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was glued in tight ranges throughout the day as Tokyo dealers refrained from taking new positions before the weekend, having experienced rapid volatility during the week. \par \par \uc2  "There was not much energy left for Tokyo players to take new positions after seeing the dollar plunging to 118.90 yen (on Wednesday) and the euro powering up towards parity (to $0.9944 on Wednesday)," a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  "With nervousness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  intact, the market hesitated to drive the dollar lower today," the dealer said. "But as there are still many uncertainties, the dollar could come under more pressure if U.S. stocks plunge again." \par \par \uc2  The dollar stayed around 119.40-119.50 yen throughout the day, keeping some distance from its seven-month low of 118.90 hit on Wednesday. As of 0541 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 119.46/51 yen, little changed from 119.55/60 yen in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly rose above 99 cents in early trade but fell back to stand at 98.78/83. Europe's common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 118.07/16 yen, little changed from late U.S. levels around 118.11. \par \par \uc2  Downward pressure on the dollar was strong, with plenty of speculators waiting to sell should it rise on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heavy sell orders placed above 120 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Many exporters were rumoured to be lowering their offer levels from above 121 yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off a barrage of Japanese economic indicators, which drew a mixed picture of the economy. \par \par \uc2  On the bright side, industrial production rose 3.9 percent in May from April, beating expectations centred on 2.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the outlook is cloudy, with the government expecting production to remain flat in June and decline slightly in July. \par \par \uc2  "May figures were pretty strong. Still, at this moment, we cannot be too optimistic," said Mari Iwashita, an economist at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  U.S. COMMITMENT \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors were trying to find out the U.S. administration's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy from key officials. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was weighed down by a widespread view in the market that the Bush administration's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  is different from the Clinton administration's," said Kazunari Kobayashi, managing director at State Street Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President George W. Bush inherited a "strong-dollar policy" from the Clinton administration but many dealers suspect the Bush team is happy to see a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Many people think the Bush administration approves of a weaker dollar to help U.S. industries," said Kobayashi. \par \par \uc2  Such a view was reinforced when Bush said on Wednesday that the dollar would seek its level based on market forces. \par \par \uc2  Dealers took his comments as an acceptance of the dollar's fall since April. It has lost more than 10 percent of its value against both the euro and the yen. \par \par \uc2  White House economic advisor Lawrence Lindsey on Thursday said the U.S. supported a strong dollar but added that markets should determine its value. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SCARES? \par \par \uc2  The dollar was supported by expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's strength just as it has done several times over the last two months. \par \par \uc2  But dealers are increasingly sceptical about the effectiveness of such steps as the dollar has continued to drop even after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's fall won't be stopped by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if both the U.S. and Europe are welcoming the dollar's fall," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  European officials have repeatedly made clear that they would welcome a rise in the euro. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said on Thursday he was not worried by the sharp appreciation in the euro and the fall in U.S. share prices, describing the movements as an expected correction. \par \par \uc2  "We always said that the euro was undervalued against the dollar...now there is a correction, not a crisis," Welteke said. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers think the euro's rise will continue - most likely to parity against the dollar in the very near future. \par \par \uc2  The dollar could fall against the yen, too, possibly beyond its recent floor of 118.90, as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone can only slow down, not stop, its decline, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors were on the sidelines following this week's volatility and reflecting recent weakness in domestic share prices, but their interest in the euro could be increasing, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Investors may be shifting their interest towards increasing euro-denominated bonds, with strong downward pressure on the dollar," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at a Japanese securities firm. \par \par \uc2  "But as (Japanese) stock prices have been drifting down recently, investors could be less aggressive about increasing foreign assets in their portfolios," the manager added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0557 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 27 Jun.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9877   0.9875   +0.02    +4.01   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               119.45   119.68   -0.19    +4.37   114.45\par  Euro/yen              117.99   117.92   +0.06    +8.54   108.71\par  Dlr/swiss             1.4901   1.4874   +0.18    -6.94   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr               1.5263   1.5288   -0.16    +1.75   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5121   1.5105   +0.11    +1.39   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.5646   0.5637   +0.16    +0.93   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4725   1.4700   +0.17    -3.26   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6469   0.6455   +0.22    +2.28   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020628dy6s00cdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
