\par\par \b \uc2  Treasurys Mixed, Trade Quiet In Tokyo After Volatile Wed \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2002\par 09:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Treasurys were mixed in quiet trade Thursday in Tokyo as dealers took a breather after a volatile session Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0650 GMT (2:50 a.m. EDT) the 10-year note was up 7/32 at 101 10/32 to yield 4.70%. The 30-year issue was last trading down 3/32 at 99 5/32 to yield 5.43%. \par \par \uc2  "The market is regaining calm," a brokerage dealer said. Prices soared Wednesday, prompted by news of improper accounting by U.S. telecommunications giant WorldCom Inc. (WCOM). \par \par \uc2  Treasurys players continue to focus on the performance of stocks and short-term notes will likely be supported for now, said the dealer. "If Treasurys lose support, then the markets will fear that it's a flight from all U.S. dollar assets," he said. \par \par \uc2  He added that dealers limited their Treasurys trade during Tokyo hours as they remain cautious that the Japanese authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the dollar moving below Y120. On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen just above Y120. \par \par \uc2  Reaction to the Federal Open Market Committee's decision to keep policy unchanged was muted as the no-change vote was widely expected. \par \par \uc2  Treasurys players are now looking ahead to U.S. first quarter final gross domestic product data to be released later Thursday and its impact on stocks. \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to believe that the stocks have hit bottom yesterday - it's hard to confirm that in just one or two days," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Prices at 0650 GMT:\par    3 1/4%  2-year   100 29/32  Dn  2/32  2.76%\par    4 3/8%  5-year   101 20/32  Dn  2/32  4.00%\par    4 7/8%  10-year  101 10/32  Up  7/32  4.70%\par    5 3/8%  30-year   99  5/32  Dn  3/32  5.43%\par    2-30-Yr Yield Spread: 267 BPS Vs 269 BPS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the Chicago Board of Trade, the September bond futures contract was\par at 103 26/32, down 13/32 from the previous session. The most-heavily\par traded March Eurodollar contract on the Singapore Exchange was at 97.31,\par down from 97.365 Wednesday at the Chicago close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Asako Tanabe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par asako.tanabe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1079 4041 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020627dy6r000g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
