\par\par \b \uc2  Standing against tide, Japan sells yen for dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoko Nishikawa \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2002\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 26 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday for a second time this week, selling yen in a campaign to prevent the tumbling dollar from derailing an export-led economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  As a slide in the dollar to 7-= month lows drove the yen up towards a psychologically crucial level of 120 per dollar, the Bank of Japan stepped into the market on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which immediately confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar skidded after U.S. telecoms giant WorldCom's admission that it had inflated its profits and on doubts over Washington's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after President George W. Bush said the dollar would seek its level based on market forces. \par \par \uc2  The slide in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was inching the euro close to parity against the dollar, continued despite several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which began when the dollar hit 120.16 yen in Tokyo afternoon trading, a 7-= month low. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times after initially buying dollars around 120.20-120.30 yen in what dealers characterised as heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the BOJ could have bought more than $4 billion. \par \par \uc2  In European business, the dollar tumbled even further against the yen to 119.98 by 1040 GMT, underscoring the fraught task facing Japanese authorities as they stand against the tide. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts expect the Bank of Japan to continue buying dollars and selling yen to prevent a move into the 115-120 yen range - levels that could force major exporters to start revising down their profit forecasts. \par \par \uc2  FURTHER LOSSES \par \par \uc2  Dealers in London said further dollar losses seemed likely as futures markets were pointing to a bloodbath on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  "We took appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today just as the day before yesterday," Haruhiko Kuroda, vice finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The yen retreated to 121.35 after the BOJ acted in what was believed to be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sixth yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late May when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid below 124 yen. \par \par \uc2  The MOF confirmed further second and third rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as the yen began clawing back up. \par \par \uc2  Referring to recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said: "It's not Japan's problem alone. \par \par \uc2  "The movements have become more complicated against the dollar and the euro and we need to closely watch movements of other nations," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  His comments were in line with Monday's statement, in which Shiokawa confirmed Japan's action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and stressed that rapid dollar/yen movements could have undesirable impact on the Japanese economy as well as the world economy. \par \par \uc2  When \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May and earlier this month, Shiokawa's statement only said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were too rapid without pointing the impact on the global economies. \par \par \uc2  NO REQUEST TO U.S. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa, however, said he had not asked the United States to help with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen about 11.3 percent against the dollar since April 1 - a worry for the government, which has spent an estimated $25 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets trying to hold it down in the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have been warning almost on a daily basis that volatility in exchange rates is undesirable and that they would take "appropriate action" if needed. \par \par \uc2  Still, Wednesday's action came as a surprise to some traders, who had expected the government to keep a low profile during the two-day Group of Eight summit meeting in Canada which began on Wednesday, given the political sensitivity of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. \par \par \uc2  Bush's administration is facing political pressure from domestic manufacturers to abandon its "strong dollar" policy, but at the same time concern is growing that a weaker dollar could halt international investment flows into the United States which are needed to fund its yawning current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  U.S. officials have also warned Japan against relying on a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports instead of squarely addressing the deep-rooted problems in its economy. \par \par \uc2  "Japan is in a real problem and it's not clear that they will be able to get out given their inflexibility," U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill said during questioning after a speech at a U.S. university. \par \par \uc2  (Additional reporting by Tamawa Kadoya). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020626dy6q00u9y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
