\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Govt Bonds End Higher Amid Stock Fall, Yen Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2002\par 08:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese government bonds advanced in a flight to quality Wednesday as stocks fell and the yen rose in the wake of the discovery of massive corporate fraud at WorldCom Inc. \par \par \uc2  Lead September 10-year JGB futures finished up 0.18 at 139.07, slightly off the intraday high of 139.12. \par \par \uc2  Higher futures prices helped lift cash bonds, traders said. The 10-year JGB yield fell 0.5 basis point to 1.315% and the five-year yield was also down one basis point at 0.42%. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock index fell about 4% to close at 10074.56. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled as news emerged of what may be one of the largest corporate frauds in history at U.S. telecommunications company WorldCom. \par \par \uc2  WorldCom discovered some $3.6 billion in expenses which were improperly booked as capital expenditure. It said the financial gimmick boosted the firm's cash flow and profits over the past five quarters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar plunge prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry Of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market via the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  invited some selling in JGBs, which proved short-lived and of little impact, said a JGB dealer at a city bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The stronger yen and weaker stocks increased uncertainty over Japan's economic outlook, sparking a shift of funds into bonds. \par \par \uc2  "Dealers are focusing on U.S. stocks, and U.S. Treasurys. The current situation makes it difficult for (JGB) dealers to sell," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stock markets will likely dictate bond market activity for now, he\par added.\par    Tiffe Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Price:   99.895  Unchanged\par    SGX Dec 3-Mos Euroyen Price:     99.895  Up 0.005\par    TSE Sep 5-Yr JGB Future Price:   N/A     N/A\par    TSE Sep 10-Yr JGB Future Price:  139.07  Up 0.18\par    SGX Sep 10-Yr JGB Future Price:  139.08  Up 0.21\par    10-Yr 1.3% JGB No. 240 Yield:    1.315%  Dn 0.005\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no reaction in the bond market to the BOJ policy board\par meeting leaving the current super-easy policy unchanged as the decision\par was widely expected and already factored in. The board voted unanimously\par to keep policy unchanged as well as to keep the current account balance\par target at Y10 trillion to Y15 trillion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the 10-year yield heads down toward 1.3%, bond market players are\par recalling the market situation about a year ago, when the 10-year JGB\par futures marked 1.13% on June 28, 2001. The yield turned up the next day\par to 1.21%, and following the BOJ tankan business survey on July 2 has\par stayed above the level since.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bonds tend to rise during the April-June quarter as new funds for the\par fiscal year starting April are invested.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This year, the June tankan survey is scheduled for release July 1 and\par market players are cautious over whether history will repeat itself,\par said Nikko Salomon Smith Barney chief strategist Kazuhiko Sano.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The June tankan is expected to show business sentiment at large\par companies has improved from the March survey but is still far from\par strong given growing uncertainties about the U.S. economic recovery and\par weak fixed investment, Sano said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market players sense the situation is different from last year but\par still remain cautious with the 10-year yield moving just above 1.3%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Excessive weakness in the stock market is often said to be a JGB\par negative as it lowers investors risk-taking ability, but as there's\par still time before the mid-fiscal year book closing at the end of\par September, the market isn't likely to see massive JGB selling due to\par this factor, Sano said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the yen interest rate swaps market, there were some position\par adjustment moves and the curve flattened as the long-term swap rates\par moved lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Both outright and spread trades were done near the bottom of recent\par ranges, but the market lacks the momentum for an attempt to break out on\par the downside, said traders, given expectations for more volatility in\par bond and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets ahead of the Federal Open Market\par Committee meeting and the Group of Eight summit in Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Asako Tanabe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par asako.tanabe@dowjones.com (With contributions from Hiroshi Miwa.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1037 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020626dy6q001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
