\par\par \b \uc2  Japan acts in bid to stop yen rise hurting recovery. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 24 (Reuters) - The Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, buying dollars for yen to prevent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising too far, too fast and derailing a fragile, export-fuelled economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, acting as the government's agent, bought dollars in the afternoon for the first time since June 4, as the greenback threatened to revisit seven-month lows hit on Friday against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the dollar more than a yen in Asian trade but it was back down to 121.35 yen by 0900 GMT, only a shade above the 121.10 to 121.20 yen level at which the Bank of Japan had stepped in, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We have taken appropriate action today in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said in a statement. "We will continue to closely monitor the market and take appropriate action as necessary." \par \par \uc2  "Recent rapid movements of the dollar-yen exchange rates in the markets could have undesirable implications for the Japanese economy and the world economy," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said it was hard to estimate how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent. They said it bought dollars in blocks of $500 million, compared with $200-400 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month. But the action was over quickly, lasting less than 30 minutes compared with several hours last time, they said. \par \par \uc2  Before Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at least four times since the dollar slid below 124 yen in late May, spending well over two trillion yen ($16.4 billion). \par \par \uc2  MORE ACTION EXPECTED \par \par \uc2  On Friday, Shiokawa said his ministry had no power to dominate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, triggering a tumble in the dollar to a seven-month low of 120.80 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was moving back down towards that level on Monday, trading at a low of 121.02 against the yen before the Bank of Japan stepped in to buy dollars, driving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as 122.80 yen at one point. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it would be difficult to change the dollar's underlying trend, given its bearishness against most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But they added that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent dramatic movements. \par \par \uc2  Last week the dollar lost more than 2.5 percent against the euro and 2.25 percent versus the yen. On Monday, the dollar hit its lowest level against the euro in more than two years. \par \par \uc2  Japan is concerned that a steep dollar slide could harm the competitiveness of Japanese exports, choking off a fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The yen has rebounded 11 percent from a 39-month low on January 31, notching the bulk of the gains since April. \par \par \uc2  "I had expected the authorities to come in at some time today, but the action may have its limitations. The authorities will likely keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a unilateral basis when the yen shoots up," said Sumitomo Mitsui Bank market analyst Daisuke Uno. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said recent movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates had been excessive. "We are closely watching the markets to see how to respond. The moves were rather rapid," he said. \par \par \uc2  His stance was echoed in the evening by Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Muto, who said other countries shared Japan's view that a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was desirable. \par \par \uc2  "The authorities have indicated they do not want to see a fall below 120 yen for now, but it will be a battle as dollar-selling pressure continues," said Yasuharu Tsuru, a manager at Mitsubishi Trust and Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  "Today's action seems to be more of a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  SHORING UP STOCKS \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been hurt by weak U.S. stock prices and news last Thursday that the U.S. current account deficit widened to record levels in the first quarter of the year, meaning the United States must attract more capital flows to fund it. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped shore up Japanese stock prices, encouraging bargain-hunters to pick up blue-chip exporters such as Sony Corp and reversing early losses in Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei closed up 116.97 points or 1.13 percent at 10,471.32 after touching a four-month intraday low of 10,169.07 in the morning session. The broader, capital-weighted TOPIX index of all first-section issues rose 1.09 percent to 1,013.23. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slightly eased pressure on exporters and gave a buy signal to bargain-hunters," said Hiroshi Sato, equities general manager at Cosmo Securities. \par \par \uc2  Consumer electronics giant Sony, which gets two-thirds of its revenues from overseas, rose 2.16 percent to 6,150 yen after hitting a four-month low of 5,910 soon after the opening. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020624dy6o00u41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
